<h2 id="cotangent-section-atiyah" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="09DC">92.17</span> The Atiyah class of a module</h2>

<p>
Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $M$ be a $B$-module. Let $P \to B$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}_{B/A}$ (Section <a href="/tag/08PQ" data-tag="08PQ">92.4</a>). Consider the extension of principal parts 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \Omega _{P/A} \otimes _ P M \to P^1_{P/A}(M) \to M \to 0  \]
</div>
<p>
 see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/09CN" data-tag="09CN">10.133.6</a>. This sequence is functorial in $P$ by Algebra, Remark <a href="/tag/09CP" data-tag="09CP">10.133.7</a>. Thus we obtain a short exact sequence of sheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \Omega _{\mathcal{O}/\underline{A}} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \underline{M} \to P^1_{\mathcal{O}/\underline{A}}(M) \to \underline{M} \to 0  \]
</div>
<p>
 on $\mathcal{C}_{B/A}$. We have $L\pi _!(\Omega _{\mathcal{O}/\underline{A}} \otimes _\mathcal {O} \underline{M}) = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B M = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} M$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/08PT" data-tag="08PT">92.4.2</a> and the flatness of the terms of $L_{B/A}$. We have $L\pi _!(\underline{M}) = M$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/08QE" data-tag="08QE">92.4.4</a>. Thus a distinguished triangle 
</p>
<div class="equation" id="09DD">
    <span class="equation-label"><a href="/tag/09DD" data-tag="09DD">92.17.0.1</a></span>
  <div>\begin{equation}  \label{cotangent-equation-atiyah} L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} M \to L\pi _!\left(P^1_{\mathcal{O}/\underline{A}}(M)\right) \to M \to L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} M [1] \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p>
 in $D(B)$. Here we use Cohomology on Sites, Remark <a href="/tag/09CZ" data-tag="09CZ">21.39.13</a> to get a distinguished triangle in $D(B)$ and not just in $D(A)$. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-definition" id="09DE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09DE">Definition <span data-tag="09DE">92.17.1</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $M$ be a $B$-module. The map $M \to L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} M[1]$ in (<a href="/tag/09DD" data-tag="09DD">92.17.0.1</a>) is called the <em>Atiyah class</em> of $M$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
